---
import PlayerLayout from "../layouts/PlayerLayout.astro";
---

<style is:global>
  body { background: var(--ground); }
</style>

<PlayerLayout title="Privacy · sleepcast">
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl px-6 pb-16 pt-[calc(2.5rem+env(safe-area-inset-top,0px))] text-[var(--ink-2)]">
    <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--ink-3)] hover:text-[var(--ink)]">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6" /></svg>
      Back to Sleepcast
    </a>

    <h1 class="mt-8 text-[32px] font-extrabold leading-tight tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] text-[var(--ink-3)]">How Sleepcast handles your data.</p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Sleepcast uses Google Analytics to understand how the site is used, to keep it running well, and to get a rough
        picture of who uses it: how many people visit, which features they reach, what devices and browsers they use, and
        the general region they connect from. This is used for running the site and deciding what to build, not to identify
        individual people.
      </p>
      <p>
        Analytics is off unless you allow it, when Sleepcast first asks or later. If you allow it, Google Analytics sets
        cookies and collects usage and approximate-location data on Google's behalf. That data is handled under
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)] underline underline-offset-2">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        You can opt out across all sites with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)] underline underline-offset-2">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>,
        or by blocking cookies for this site. Sleepcast still works fully with analytics blocked.
      </p>
      <p>
        <span id="sc-consent-status"></span>
        <button id="sc-consent-reset" type="button" class="ml-1 font-semibold text-[var(--ink)] underline underline-offset-2">Change your choice</button>
        <span class="text-[var(--ink-3)]">(asks again, and removes Google Analytics' cookies)</span>
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Your shows, timer settings, listening positions, nights and play history live in your browser's storage on your
        own device. They aren't uploaded to a Sleepcast account, because there is no account.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Audio and feeds</h2>
      <p>
        Episodes are fetched from their original podcast feeds. When a request needs to pass through Sleepcast's relay,
        the specific episode address isn't logged.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Finding podcasts</h2>
      <p>
        Searching for a podcast sends the words you type to Apple's podcast directory, through sleepcast.pro, so Apple
        sees Cloudflare's address and not yours. Nothing else goes with them, and sleepcast.pro doesn't log them. The
        results' artwork comes the same way. The hand-picked catalog and adding a show by its link send nothing.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">No ads, no selling data</h2>
      <p>
        Sleepcast doesn't run advertising and doesn't sell your data. Analytics exists to run and improve the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Children</h2>
      <p>
        Sleepcast is for people 13 and over. On a first visit it asks when you were born, and keeps only whether you're
        old enough (and, if not, when you answered), on your device; the date itself isn't stored or sent anywhere. Under
        13, the app doesn't open and analytics never loads. A wrong date can be entered again a day later.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:nathanib@pm.me" class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)] underline underline-offset-2">nathanib@pm.me</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-12 text-[13px] text-[var(--ink-3)]">Last updated November 2026</p>
  </main>
</PlayerLayout>
